// ============================================================================
// Interactions in the bar (Chapter 2): one knot per interactable in
// src/data/areas/borderland/bar.ts. Draft text for the designer to rewrite.
// ============================================================================

=== bar_stage ===
A corner for music. Strings across an old casing; it sounds better than it should.
-> END

=== bar_table ===
A crew's table, their mark scratched into the top. They stop talking when you get close.
-> END

=== bar_counter ===
The counter is one piece, curved, with no joins anywhere. Nobody's ever found another like it.
Elbows have polished a stripe along the top.
-> END

=== bar_booths ===
The booths, curtains half drawn. Voices, low. Whatever's said up here isn't said downstairs.
-> END

// --- People (draft) ---

=== bar_barkeep ===
"Drink, or are you just here for the gossip? Everyone's here for the gossip." #speaker:barkeep
-> END

=== bar_friend ===
"There you are! Sit, sit. You look like the fields chewed you up." #speaker:scav_friend
"Me? Nothing. Early night." #speaker:scav_friend
-> END

=== bar_old_scav ===
"Hmph. You. Still digging where everyone's already dug?" #speaker:old_scav
"Dig where it's dangerous, or dig for nothing. Those are your choices." #speaker:old_scav
-> END
